yeah  [Music]  it's that time again Sony have announced  the PS plus essential offerings for  October 2022. as always you can grab  these games from the first Tuesday of  the month which this time is October the  4th this month we have a brutal fighter  a teeny tiny racer and a matrix inspired  first-person shooter so let's do this we  begin with Injustice 2. this fighting  game may be five years old but it still  holds up superbly well to this day  almost every issue players had with Gods  Among Us has been addressed Injustice 2  is faster than Injustice 1. with better  use of combos more environmental  interactions more super moves unique to  each character and of course it just  looks more impressive an impressive  update is based around managing a meter  to get the edge in battle use a portion  of your bar to become briefly immune to  those annoying people who throw out the  same projectile move over and over again  that meter can be used for far more than  that so be sure to get to know it as  soon as you can to get the most out of  Injustice 2. the story mode campaign  attempts to tell a story about  Superman's fall and becoming a tyrant  but it's a little too depressing if I'm  honest and it becomes a chore rather  than a highlight to play through kinda  like the movies the Multiverse mode is  another highlight as we complete daily  challenges to level up characters and  change their Aesthetics to stand out  from the crowd making your fighter look  how you choose once you unlock that  piece of clothing Injustice 2 received 9  out of 10 reviews across the board from  all major outlets and since then the  Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles have been  added to make the roster absolutely  enormous game number two has both PS4  and PS5 versions Hot Wheels Unleashed  another amazing game that you need to  try an arcade racer on a tiny scale that  feels like you're traveling at 100 miles  an hour when in fact you could walk  quicker the tracks weave Under and Over  household items in someone's kitchen  bedroom and living room the more aware  players will find cheeky shortcuts over  countertops and under tables to reduce  the car boss driving towards a  basketball and realizing it's not as big  as a house you're in a toy car it all  adds to the character of Hot Wheels  Unleashed if you ever owned a Hot Wheels  car there's a chance you'll find it in  the game including some huge tie-ins  such as the Delorean from Back to the  Future online sessions support 12  players for some crazy game nights with  friends or there's a split screen mode  for couch Co-op if that's more your  speed and for Creative people there is a  very competent track Creator to do with  whatever you want reviewers tell us we  should play Hot Wheels Unleashed  averaging an 8 out of 10 score and  finally super hot a first person puzzle  shooter not to be confused with the  brilliant VR game of the same Name the  basic premise is simple time only moves  when you move allowing us to survey our  attackers and plan the perfect way to  take them all down without being shot  and should we be shot the entire Scene  resets It honestly feels like a training  scene from The Matrix with a long red  line depicting bullet velocity as you  slowly wander around this before the  action kicks in super hot demands  accurate shooting in the later stages  and using inanimate objects to your  advantage the end of the game is pretty  tricky too but that's a conversation for  another time right now you just need to  decide if you're gonna try it so what do  you think happy sad delighted mad sound  off in the comments below I'm Adam I'm  definitely gonna play Hot Wheels  Unleashed it's been a pleasure I'll see  you next time  [Music]

